WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:05.880
In 2017, fans of creepy clown hijinks rushed
to the theater, breaking box office records

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:09.940
in a rush to see the remake of It, adapted
from the Stephen King book of the same name.

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:13.660
The film was met with wide acclaim and hailed
as a new classic... but just because something

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:16.420
is awesome doesn't mean it can't be kind of
stupid, too.

00:00:16.609 --> 00:00:20.480
Despite its iconic scenes, killer writing,
and knockout performances, It has its share

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:22.120
of moments that left us scratching our heads.

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:24.060
Georgie who?

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:28.860
If you know anyone who lost a sibling growing
up, you're probably very aware that it's a

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:33.660
devastating blow that can tear apart both
families and communities... except in Derry.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.720
In Derry, you mostly shrug it off and make
fun of your friend's mom.

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:40.480
When Georgie goes missing, the only people
who seem torn up about it are Bill and his

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:40.980
dad.

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:41.980
Probably his mom, too.

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:46.760
Her entire contribution seems to be providing
incidental piano music for her youngest to

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:48.200
get eaten by a clown to.

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:52.560
Everyone deals with tragedy in their own way,
but none of the kids seem to do much to process

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:56.120
the fact that a little boy straight up disappeared
into the great unknown.

00:00:57.160 --> 00:00:57.880
Detective Ben

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:00.400
That Benjamin is a heck of a dude.

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:03.020
He's got an eye for detail and an inquisitive
mind.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:06.890
Would you believe he was the first person
in all of Derry's history to notice there's

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:10.159
an inexplicable disaster every 27 years?

00:01:10.159 --> 00:01:15.510
How is it that, in a town that's been around
for, presumably, about 260 years, the first

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:18.500
person to notice this trend is a bored kid
on summer break?

00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:21.939
None of the cops or teachers or historians
in this town has ever been thumbing through

00:01:21.940 --> 00:01:26.360
A History of Derry and noticed that kids get
killed here on an alarmingly regular basis.

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:27.700
Congratulations, kid.

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:29.420
You're this universe's Batman.

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:31.380
Librarian hubris

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:35.940
We find Ben in the library, studying up on
possible past It encounters.

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:36.880
He's learning.

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:37.660
That's good.

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:39.020
We want him in the library.

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:43.480
There's only one person who doesn't want him
in the library, and that's the librarian.

00:01:43.480 --> 00:01:44.540
"Isn't it summer vacation?

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:47.340
I'd think you'd be ready to take a break from
the books"

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:51.120
She kicks a quietly studious child out of
the library.

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:51.620
You know.

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:52.940
Like librarians do.

00:01:53.260 --> 00:01:58.080
Was there really a point in history when librarians
were so secure in the idea that libraries

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:01.260
would be around forever that they'd shoo inquisitive
patrons out the door?

00:02:01.480 --> 00:02:05.160
If she's still working today, she probably
looks back longingly on the days when you

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:08.860
could evict someone from the library for something
besides trying to live in the bathroom.

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:11.000
History class

00:02:11.540 --> 00:02:15.220
Take a look at Ben's bedroom: it's got pictures
and newspaper clippings lining the walls.

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:17.260
And, well, this.

00:02:17.569 --> 00:02:21.400
How he got all of this information home when
he apparently can't leave the library without

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:24.180
getting mugged is a mystery in itself, but
that isn't the point.

00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:26.080
Who shows up in an illustration?

00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:30.090
You'd better believe it's Pennywise, in a
print of the signing of Derry's town charter.

00:02:30.090 --> 00:02:34.650
But It showing up in an old image means one
of two things: Either It is doing his usual

00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:38.990
routine of projecting into places he shouldn't
be, or else It was there at Town Hall in the

00:02:38.990 --> 00:02:44.280
late 1700s and not only did nobody mention
or object to it, but he just barely warranted

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:47.290
making it into the 18th-century equivalent
of the group photo.

00:02:47.290 --> 00:02:48.900
How could you forget that face?

00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:50.780
Who taught you murder?

00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:54.660
As far as we know, It has one job: eatin'
kids.

00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:56.000
That's It's whole deal.

00:02:56.180 --> 00:02:59.080
It's been popping up every 27 years to do
just that.

00:02:59.140 --> 00:03:00.500
So why is he so bad at it?

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:01.820
How many kids does he kill?

00:03:01.940 --> 00:03:02.440
Two?

00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:04.160
Maybe four, depending on how you count?

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:08.000
The children of Derry would've been in more
danger if a bad flu had hit the town.

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:09.760
And what about the bullies that It eliminated?

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:14.180
In a way, It saved more lives than he took
by nipping those pieces of work in the bud.

00:03:14.180 --> 00:03:15.100
Pick a lane, Pennywise.

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:17.960
There's the argument that It feeds on children's
fear.

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:22.280
Two counterpoints: First, in a much more literal
sense, he feeds on children.

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:26.659
Secondly, in the book, It refers to causing
fear as more of a way of "salting the meat,"

00:03:26.660 --> 00:03:29.500
which means this dude is risking his life
to season his steak.

00:03:29.820 --> 00:03:32.120
Pretty fancy for a guy who spends his time
in the sewers.

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:32.840
Speaking of...

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:34.800
Diseases of Derry

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:38.340
Let's discuss for a moment what makes sewers
so important.

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:42.579
They convey human waste, rainwater runoff,
and our ill-fated goldfish from cities to

00:03:42.580 --> 00:03:44.400
treatment plants and disposal outlets.

00:03:44.420 --> 00:03:48.740
They're more or less the key thing that separates
us from apes, but they're rife with disease.

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:52.220
And these kids are traipsing through them
like they're a McDonald's PlayPlace.

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:54.940
Sorry, every one of these kids is getting
hepatitis.

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:58.640
Eddie brings this up when they first start
exploring the Barrens, but you know what sassiness

00:03:58.640 --> 00:03:59.840
doesn't protect you from?

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:00.680
Cholera.

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:02.540
Maybe we're projecting

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:07.680
The Losers Club heads to Bill's garage, where
Bill has set up what's doomed to be the second

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:09.860
worst TED talk about clowns of all time.

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:13.599
They're flipping through slides when the slide
projector takes on a life of its own, until

00:04:13.599 --> 00:04:17.950
a series of photos of Bill and Georgie's mom
undergoes a nightmarish transformation: Mom

00:04:17.950 --> 00:04:19.540
straight up turns into Pennywise!

00:04:19.540 --> 00:04:21.759
And then nobody unplugs the projector.

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:22.680
"Turn it off.

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:24.580
Turn it off!"

00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:29.020
Mike kicks the projector off the table, but
still, nobody turns it off!

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:33.280
Everybody in the room just screams and wigs
out, failing to take their lives, or in fact

00:04:33.320 --> 00:04:35.280
the power cord, into their own hands.

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:37.160
Ben's got guts

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:41.770
Tough guy Ben walks off an astonishing number
of gut injuries in this movie.

00:04:41.770 --> 00:04:45.500
First, the bullies try to carve their name
into him with a switchblade, which he escapes

00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:49.410
by tumbling down a dirt hill and trouncing
through sewer runoff, only to have his wounds

00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:51.560
treated by children with drug store bandages.

00:04:51.949 --> 00:04:56.620
Then, in the creepy house, Ben gets slashed
in the belly by It, which he just sort of

00:04:56.620 --> 00:04:58.100
seems to ignore afterward.

00:04:58.100 --> 00:05:01.419
After that first haunted mansion encounter,
he's just standing out in the street with

00:05:01.420 --> 00:05:03.140
four foot-long gashes in his abdomen.

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:05.400
You could maybe see his appendix if you squint.

00:05:05.640 --> 00:05:08.919
It's worth pointing out that during that whole
scene, Eddie's mom is standing in front of

00:05:08.919 --> 00:05:13.220
Ben watching him bleed from his torso, and
she thinks it's more important to shame a

00:05:13.220 --> 00:05:14.940
12-year-old than it is to find him a doctor.

00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:16.540
The adults in this town are a mess.

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:18.400
Defying death

00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:21.580
In a lot of ways, It isn't supposed to make
sense.

00:05:21.580 --> 00:05:23.960
It's a piece of horror fiction that deals
in the supernatural.

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:27.760
But still, there's one thing that really,
truly doesn't make any sense.

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:32.100
Specifically, how are those insanely self-destructive
bullies still alive?

00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:35.640
All we see them do in this movie is take needless
risks for two hours.

00:05:35.650 --> 00:05:38.639
They drive blindly down alleyways at breakneck
speed.

00:05:38.639 --> 00:05:40.630
They make flamethrowers out of cans of hairspray.

00:05:40.630 --> 00:05:44.200
They dive headfirst down steep hills covered
in debris.

00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:45.720
They play with loaded guns.

00:05:46.120 --> 00:05:47.620
They're the definition of awful.

00:05:47.840 --> 00:05:50.780
It shouldn't have taken an extradimensional
demon to beat these jerks.

00:05:51.050 --> 00:05:54.580
With their behavior, every one of them should've
been a full-color "In Loving Memory" page

00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:56.280
in the yearbook by their sophomore year.

